From 1994354457984e2d74e2529e71429bcf9a12cce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): optimize DeepSeek V4.1 tokenizer, stop priming,
 and tool serving

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0810.

Rationale: Speeds up DeepSeek V4.1 prompt encoding and tool rendering on long
conversations, bounds FastIncrementalDetokenizer stop-string priming to the
UTF-8-aligned prompt suffix window, escapes literal image tokens in user text,
and preserves inline defer_loading and tool_reference discovery in Anthropic
serving while guarding None text and Mapping content blocks.

Quality implications: None; token equivalence across 64K-256K prompts, UTF-8
suffix alignment, literal image token preservation, and Anthropic tool-reference
conversion are verified by unit tests.

Tests: pytest -q -p deepseek_models tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py
tests/detokenizer/test_check_stop_strings.py
tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py (sync tests).

Upstream status: local candidate-60 patch
